WEBVTT

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.120
Excuse me, Sherlock!

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:36.290
M-Miss Hudson, you are looking exceptionally
beautiful on this most glorious of days...

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.200
All right, then, good day.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.750
Just a moment!

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.450
Here!

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.870
Woof!

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.790
Don't you bark at me, you ne'er-do-well!

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.830
I just need a little longer!
Really, just a little!

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.410
I've grown weary of hearing you say that!

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.700
If you don't have the money, then get a job!

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.660
And if you can't do that, I am kicking
you out of the room, understand?!

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.580
It isn't like that, Miss Hudson!

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.750
You know that my job is unique,
don't you?! Waiting sort of <i>is </i>my job!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.580
--Huh?!
--Holmes! Holmes, right?

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.540
What are you shouting about
out here in the road?

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.040
Stamford!

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.410
Miss Hudson, this is my good friend...

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:24.290
The name is Stamford. I'm a doctor
at St Bartholomew's Hospital.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:26.450
Oh, it's a pleasure to meet you.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.660
Now that that's settled... lend me some money.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.580
I see, so that is the situation.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.200
I truly am at my wits' end!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.790
Oh, Miss Hudson, being cross
will give you wrinkles.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.910
What did you say?! And just whose
fault is it that I am cross?!

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:53.500
Now, now. What if you were to find a flatmate
for Holmes, one who would split the rent?

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.620
Flatmate?

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.000
<i>The mist is hiding the sin</i>

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.750
<i>I hold in my hand the LIST of judgment</i>

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.370
<i>I'm gonna do the perfect crime</i>
<i>and bury them in a cist</i>

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:18.620
<i>That's my DYING WISH for you</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:24.040
<i>Guys of the privileged class torment the weak</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.120
<i>And they enjoy it</i>

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.660
<i>That's a bloody world, an endlessly</i>
<i>discriminatory society (dystopia)</i>

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:37.700
<i>Happiness does not bloom here</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.830
<i>We are oppressed</i>

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:46.410
<i>We must do something. Come on</i>

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:52.870
<i>Let the end begin</i>

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:58.700
<i>Break it to relieve your soul</i>

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:04.620
<i>Open your eyes. You'll be reborn</i>
<i>when you lose your life</i>

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:09.700
<i>We're lords of crime. We're sacrifice for ideals</i>

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:22.000
<i>Freedom lives forever, even if we die</i>

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.450
"A Study in 'S' Act 1"

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.540
"A Study in 'S' Act 1"

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.540
So now, I have brought some candidates
to share the room with me.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:34.700
So now, I have brought some candidates
to share the room with me.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.750
Would you care to choose one?

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:40.290
So it's an audition, is it? Of course I will.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.660
All right, here is the first one.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:50.370
Hey. What do I do for a living?
Right now, I'm still a struggling actor.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.750
You want to be my patron?
I'll pay you for the rent when I make it big.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.200
I'm afraid I can't do that.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:03.200
I heard you wouldn't mind if I brought men
back to my room for my work. Is this true?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.750
Out of the question, obviously!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:09.200
Did I hear something about living for free
in a home with a roof over it?

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.160
You have no intention of paying at all, do you?!

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.540
Huh?

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.330
Stop monkeying with me!
Those people are obviously unfit!

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.790
This is intentional!
You're doing this intentionally!

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:24.700
If you don't arrange something,
I will kick you out of here!

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:32.370
I've nowhere else to turn. Stamford,
isn't there anything you can do?

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.580
Well, this is all so sudden.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:40.040
Hold on a moment. <i>He </i>might be willing...

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.410
Baker Street, 221B.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.370
This is the place.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:08.620
No one home? I'm right on time.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.790
Begging your pardon--

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.370
What is that odour?

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:20.700
Excuse me, is anyone at home?

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.290
Excuse me!

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.000
You there! Are you all right?!

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.080
His pulse is normal... and his body
temperature is unaffected...

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.790
Nothing blocking his airway.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:47.750
There doesn't seem to be any external injury...
so where exactly is this blood from?

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.500
What... time is it?

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:57.040
Gah! It's this late already?! I fell asleep!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.200
Huh? Uh, are you all right? All this blood...

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.040
Oh, this? It's cow blood.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:09.750
Oh, fantastic! There's a reaction!
Yes! It's a success!

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:11.700
What is?

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:16.200
This is a new agent that only reacts
and precipitates with blood.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.120
Even if you have a tiny stain
from many months back,

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:23.290
this will allow you to determine
whether or not it's blood.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.950
Indeed...

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.080
Once this becomes practically applied,

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.830
there are any number of murder
cases that will be overturned!

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.160
The tincture of guaiac method,
which is similar to this,

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.410
is not only fallible, it's also a lot of work,
and takes a fair bit of time.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.200
But this is--

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.580
Who are you?

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:49.200
Pardon me. I'm John H. Watson.
Are you Sherlock Holmes?

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.160
--My friend Stamford says
that you have a room to let--

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:52.910
--Hmm...
--My friend Stamford says
that you have a room to let--

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.000
You're a doctor, back from the Afghan War.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.330
How did you know that...?

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.910
By simple deduction.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:03.120
You wasted no time in coming over
to me where I was collapsed,

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:07.000
took my pulse, and tried to clear my airway.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.370
Those are the actions of someone
trained in the medical arts.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:13.910
Then, there are the signs of a nasty sunburn.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.750
You don't get a burn like that
in London this time of year.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:23.500
You were stationed as a medic in
Afghanistan and are now retired.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:28.000
The pocket watch I checked earlier is one
that is issued upon discharge from the army.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.620
Living in a hotel in London
is tight on a soldier's pension...

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:38.410
...so the choice of sharing
a room is more realistic.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.500
You've got me. Well deduced.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:45.500
I am indeed a former medic,
back from the Afghan War.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.200
That certainly was some
outstanding logical reasoning.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.790
Was it? Well, will you write
in your journal today,

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:55.830
"My new flatmate is a bloody amazing chap"?

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.160
You do write, don't you?

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.790
You have ink smudges on your right thumbnail.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.500
Oh, yeah...

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.870
Well, we'd best be off.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.160
Off? To where?

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.830
Our landlady, Miss Hudson,

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:13.160
has invited us to dinner,
where you two can become acquainted.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.950
I'm glad to hear it. Also, you can call me John.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:20.750
All right, John. I do not have
any issue with you,

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.200
but you will have to be screened
by our landlady, Miss Hudson.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:31.750
Very well then, to welcome my new flatmate...

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:34.660
I have not yet given my <i>okay</i>.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:38.870
N-Now, we can discuss that over our drinks.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.620
--Cheers!
--Cheers...

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:52.000
Qu-Quite the drinker, aren't you, Miss Hudson?

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.830
Yes, well, you see, Miss Hudson is
terribly careworn for some reason.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:09:00.500
And just who do you think is the source
of the majority of those cares?!

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:03.790
I-I think I have some idea why that may be.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.040
However, Sherlock possesses
some extraordinary talents.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.580
To be honest, I was left speechless
by his powers of observation

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.250
and his perspicacity, myself.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:18.000
Yes, he truly does squander his abilities.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:22.330
I only wish he would use that cunning mind
of his for the betterment of the world--

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.040
Where are you going?!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.790
Just off to the loo.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.620
Huh? Trying to run away?

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.410
I'm not running.

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:33.410
If you're anxious, we could indulge
in a communal convenience break.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.200
Sherlock!

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:39.200
Honestly, the man has nary a shred of decency.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:43.290
Miss Hudson, what sort of man is Sherlock?

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:47.450
I could not tell you! Honest to God,
I do not understand him.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:50.410
His mind is always off thinking
about something else,

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.370
and he often fails to come home
for two or three days at a time.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:58.250
Other times, he locks himself in his room
and ignores me. And for all that...

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:02.790
...once in a while, he can be very kind,
and does as I ask him to.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.660
I-In any case, he is a child!

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.200
Which is why I insist that he have someone
who's well-grounded as a housemate!

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.290
You worry about him, don't you, Miss Hudson?

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.500
Almost as though you were family.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:26.330
When Miss Hudson gets worked up
like this, she's liable to...

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.790
That actually happened to you?

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.950
--My, you really did have a time
of it on the battlefield.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.160
--Huh?
--My, you really did have a time
of it on the battlefield.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:37.580
Oh, no. Compared to the soldiers
who took up their rifles...

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:39.250
Oh, took you long enough.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:41.290
Uh, yeah...

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:45.000
The two of you seem to be
quite open with each other.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.950
Yes. Mr Watson is a very
down-to-earth gentleman.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:57.330
Forgive me for interrupting
such a merry occasion.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.200
Oh, hello.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.950
Miss Hudson, who is this?

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:07.620
This is Inspector Lestrade of Scotland Yard.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.200
The police?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:16.330
Here it comes! My case!

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.750
Your case?

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:23.370
John, this is my job. When the police
have a case that's beyond them,

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.870
I step in and solve it,
as the world's foremost...

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.750
...consulting detective!

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:33.040
Consulting...

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.410
Lestrade! What are we just standing around for?

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.540
Where is the crime scene? Let's be off at once!

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:44.370
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid we can't do that.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.410
Huh?

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:52.620
As it happens, tonight, at about 22:00,
Count Drebber was murdered.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:59.250
On the floor next to the count's body...
was a message written in blood.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:03.250
It read... "Sherlock."

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:04.660
What?

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:10.040
I'm reluctant to do this, myself...

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.330
...but Sherlock Holmes,

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:19.410
you are under arrest on suspicion
of the murder of Count Drebber.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.200
This is a masterpiece!

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:34.950
My name, written in blood?
Good show. Most amusing.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:39.450
We were all together at the estimated
time that the body expired.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.290
Which is why we're taking all of you in.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:44.830
Honestly, Scotland Yard
is always so easily fooled.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.540
That's all it took for you
to pin me as the culprit?

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:54.250
We'll see how long you can afford
to remain so insolent.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:59.290
Ho? Well, this explains it. It's you, Gregson.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:04.330
I am thrilled to finally be able
to arrest you, you bohemian.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.700
You <i>do </i>understand that it's
because of prats like you

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:10.160
that the Yard is thought
to be ineffectual, right?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:14.910
This is why you will forever
be an <i>assistant </i>inspector.

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.000
Take him away at once!

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.910
Aye, sir.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:25.750
And as for you two, I have some
questions for you, as well.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:36.370
Take a good look. This is what we found in
the residence of the suspect, Sherlock Holmes.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:40.580
The footprints left at the scene are
the same size as the suspect's,

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:45.500
and the gun is of the same calibre
as the one used in the crime.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:50.950
The suspect is also a dangerous man
who has caused trouble many times before.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:54.370
I believe the possibility that he
is the culprit is quite high.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:00.040
You swear it wasn't you, right?

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:07.000
Footprints can be faked... and my pistol
is brand new; it's never even been fired.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:10.200
Check it and you will be able
to tell straight away.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.870
This is no ordinary case.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.830
There's something huge
at work behind the scenes.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:23.040
Something that remains unseen.
We have to pin that down.

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:29.500
Lestrade, let me see the crime scene.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.910
If you say you're inspecting the scene
with the suspect, that ought to cover it.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:38.660
Holmes, don't tell me you mean
to find the true killer yourself.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:45.620
But of course. They seem to
have called me out, after all.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.620
Sherlock!

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.540
Are you all right? Miss Hudson
and I have been released.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:04.660
Glad to hear it. I trust Gregson was
bull-headed in his interrogation.

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:11.330
John, I need your help to find the true culprit.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:15.750
Mr Watson, I would like
to ask it of you, as well.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.620
If I can be of any assistance...

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:22.950
I will, Sherlock!

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:26.080
Once again, I appreciate your help, John.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:38.160
This street has nothing but
aristocrat mansions, hasn't it?

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:41.040
What are you doing? Come along, quickly!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.290
In here is Count Drebber's study.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:50.950
His body is still where we found it,
and hasn't been taken to the morgue.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:09.620
Lestrade, tell me what you know.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:14.250
His name is Enoch J. Drebber.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:17.040
Born in Wales, 35 years old.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:20.830
There are two maids and a butler
who live here in the mansion,

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:25.080
as well as an older woman in a
detached room who does the cooking.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.830
Of the two live-in maids,

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:34.500
at the estimated time of death,
one of them had a date with her lover...

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:39.500
...but despite waiting all night,
he never showed up.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:45.000
Moreover, she was the
first one to find the body.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.620
As for the other maid...

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.910
...she received word that her father
had suddenly collapsed

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:53.250
and rushed back to her parents' house...

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.000
...but her father was apparently hale and hardy.

00:16:57.290 --> 00:17:00.620
The butler is fond of drinking,
and in between his duties,

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:04.790
he typically spends his time
in his room sipping whisky,

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.450
but apparently, it had been laced
with some sort of drug,

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:11.200
and at the time of the murder,
he was sound asleep in his room.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:19.040
The older woman who is his cook is hard of
hearing, and once she locks herself in her room,

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:22.660
she wouldn't even notice
if lightning struck outside her door.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:31.200
And so, tonight, at 10:15, the maid
discovered the count slumped over.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:37.290
So you're saying that there was no one
in the mansion who heard gunshots.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:42.200
John, would you mind inspecting the body?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.580
Very well.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.250
Four gunshot wounds to the chest.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:55.370
There don't appear to be
any other signs of a struggle.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.000
Judging by the size of the gunshot wounds,

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:00.250
they were likely caused by a pistol
discharged at point-blank range.

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:03.250
They were probably aiming for the heart.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.620
Judging from the amount of blood present,

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:10.330
there is no doubt that he died of
massive blood loss from his wounds.

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:13.750
It's fair to conclude that he
died almost immediately.

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:17.120
That is all I can tell at this point.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:18.870
Sherlock?

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.750
Excellent work, John.

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.040
Is something the matter?

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.660
Oh, I thought there might be
some loose change under here.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:28.000
Why, you! Stop clowning about!

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.830
Go even a little bit easy on you
and you start your tomfoolery!

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:35.000
Lestrade, would you like me
to tell you what I've learnt?

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:40.660
Yes. Let's hear what the
consulting detective has to say.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:43.160
First, there's the writing in blood.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:47.040
The count was not the one
who wrote this--it was the culprit.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.450
What's your evidence?

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:50.830
If you look closely, it's obvious.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:55.580
The width of the lettering is thicker
than the count's bloody finger.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:19:01.080
For the count to write letters as bold as this,
he would have to trace each line twice.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:05.120
It's hard to consider that he would draw
each line twice if he were dying quickly.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:09.450
So then, the killer is someone
with fingers wider than the victim.

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:12.200
Yeah, very much so.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:15.040
Finger width is generally
proportional to hand size,

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:19.000
and hand size is generally
proportional to one's physical size.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:22.290
It stands to reason, then,
that there is a high probability

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:25.370
that the real killer is a much
larger man than the count.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.200
I see.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.790
Next is the means of killing.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:33.620
Were this a skilled killer, there would be
one shot to the head, then perhaps,

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:38.620
once taking careful aim after the first shot,
the next one would be through the heart.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:43.000
However, as you can see, you wonder
if the killer was actually aiming at all.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:45.250
I had the same thought.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:48.660
It appears that the culprit was
unskilled in handling firearms.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.700
Being unskilled is one thing,
but they missed all his vitals,

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:55.450
and it is plainly clear that
they fired blindly at him.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:58.120
They used one trick or another
to ensure the servants were away,

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:00.750
making certain everything was
arranged on a silver platter,

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:04.160
but when it came down to the
actual act, it turned out like so.

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.160
Almost as though an amateur performer
was doing their utmost

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:12.410
to follow a well-crafted script,
whilst trying to play the role of the killer.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:19.620
In other words, the one responsible for
killing Count Drebber was an amateur,

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:24.870
but there was also someone else,
much more capable, imparting their wisdom.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:30.200
So there was a mastermind, other than
the killer, who put this plan together?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.870
That's right. There's someone else in this case,

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:37.620
pulling all the strings, who came up
with this plot. It's as if...

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:43.370
Just like the case on the ship, there is a
colossal puzzle visible in the background.

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:48.450
Holmes...

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.870
Holmes!

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:55.700
So then, why did whoever told
the real culprit to write in blood...

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:57.700
...instruct them to write <i>your </i>name?

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:03.160
Search me. We'll have to catch them
and ask them why they chose me.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:06.330
Enough! I can't take any more
of your evasive doubletalk!

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:10.120
Inspector, request permission
to interrogate Holmes!

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:13.000
--I will do whatever it takes to get Holmes
to confess to his wrongdoing!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.830
--John...
--I will do whatever it takes to get Holmes
to confess to his wrongdoing!

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:30.750
So long as you can take your revenge,

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:35.200
it does not matter to you that you
may lose your life as a result.

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:38.700
Your volition remains unchanged, then?

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:41.500
Of course.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:46.540
Sooner or later, I will fall victim to this
incurable disease, and I haven't much time.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:51.750
My wish has already come true.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:53.910
My life means nothing to me.

00:21:57.410 --> 00:22:01.500
His death is near, and he
is all alone in the world.

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:05.950
He is the man best suited
to carrying out this plan.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:10.250
This will allow me to test <i>him</i>.

00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:20.200
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:24.410
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:43.500
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:45.750
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:49.290
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:52.500
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:56.000
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.620
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:03.370
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:23:03.370 --> 00:23:08.200
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:11.870
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:13.540
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:23:13.540 --> 00:23:15.330
<i>at the end</i>

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:18.500
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:22.750
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:29.370
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:30.870
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:37.700
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:43.330
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:45.700
<i>There is no turning back</i>

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:52.330
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
'A Study in "S" Act 2.'
